\par\par \b \uc2 The FT crypto glossary\b0\par\par\uc2 Philip Stafford \par \uc2 5,167 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2021\par 04:00\par \uc2 Financial Times (FT.Com)\par \uc2 FTCOM\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The Financial Times Ltd. All rights reserved. Please do not cut and paste FT articles and redistribute by email or post to the web. \par \par \uc2 Want to speak crypto? This guide tells you all you need to know\par \par \uc2 Alt or alternative coins: Any cryptocurrency other than the original cryptocurrency, Bitcoin, is known as an alt-coin. Alt-coins range from relatively well-established and popular coins like t through to joke currencies like dogecoin. The term is also sometimes applied to stablecoins or to tokens that represent a stake of ownership, such as a security token.\par \par \uc2 Automated Market Maker: An actor that encourages buyers and sellers in a decentralised market. Like market makers on traditional markets, they aim to make money from discrepancies in pricing on different markets, until the asset price falls into line across all markets. An automated market maker deposits their own pair of cryptocurrencies into a smart contract and lets computer code handle buying and selling with interested parties, who are also using their own smart contracts. Owners of assets are incentivised by sharing in the pool of fees that are generated through trading activity. The process has been compared to \uc2 YouTube\uc2  because investors can generate and upload their own content.\par \par \uc2 Automatic liquidation: A common feature in leveraged trading on a crypto exchange. A futures trader only pays for a small fraction of the overall value of their position, which is a bet on the direction of the asset. The leverage can magnify potential gains and losses. That payment, margin, is used to back the trade. In a traditional market, when the asset price goes against the direction the trader has bet, the exchange may ask the customer to stump up extra funds within a certain timeframe to keep the trade open. A position on a crypto exchange can work differently. The exchange monitors the market constantly and may automatically begin selling off some of the customer\u8217\'20\'19s bets if the customer\u8217\'20\'19s margin falls below a pre-determined level. Typically a user will receive an alert if their account is in danger \u8212\'20\'14 but given the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  of digital assets, these kinds of forced liquidation events can leave traders wiped out extremely quickly.\par \par \uc2 Bagholder: An investor who refuses to let go of a cryptocurrency despite its poor performance, delaying their exit long enough for the coin to eventually become worthless.\u160\'00\'A0\par \par \uc2 Bankman-Fried, Sam: Known widely as SBF, Bankman-Fried is the co-founder and former chief executive of the now bankrupt cryptocurrency exchange \uc2 FTX\uc2 . Once the crypto world\u8217\'20\'19s most high-profile executive, a regular lobbyist in Washington DC and with a then net worth of about $26bn, SBF fell from grace with the collapse of his company. He was then charged by the US with multiple crimes, including conspiracy to commit wire fraud, wire fraud, conspiracy to commit securities and commodities fraud and conspiracy to defraud the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Basel Committee on Banking Supervision\uc2 : The world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful standards setter for banks. It determines how banks control risks and how much equity they should hold to protect themselves if markets or customers blow up. It has proposed differing \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  categories for banks wanting to buy and sell crypto for customers or themselves. Banks can treat stock tokens and stablecoins on their balance sheets like existing assets, with some rule modifications. Bitcoin and others would come under a new \u8220\'20\'1Cconservative\u8221\'20\'1D prudential regime, so banks would need to hold at least enough equity to more than cover all potential losses.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2 : The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency exchange, founded in 2017 by \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 . The exchange says it does not have a headquarters, but semi-autonomous units that allow it to operate around the world. However it has clashed with many regulators and in March 2023 the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  sued both \uc2 Binance\uc2  and Zhao, filing a total of 13 charges. They included \uc2 Binance\uc2  operating unregistered exchanges, broker-dealers and clearing agencies as well as misrepresenting trading controls and oversight on \uc2 Binance\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US platform. \uc2 Binance\uc2  has said it will fight the suit.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin: The biggest and original cryptocurrency that launched an entire industry. It was envisaged by its pseudonymous creator (or creators) \uc2 Satoshi Nakamoto\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpeer-to-peer electronic cash system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 BNB\uc2  coin: The cryptocurrency of the exchange \uc2 Binance\uc2 . It was launched in 2017 with the promise that only 200mn tokens will ever exist. Every quarter, \uc2 Binance\uc2  uses a fifth of its profits to destroy already existing coins, in a bid to make them more scarce and in turn, more valuable. The coins can be used to pay for \uc2 Binance\uc2  services, to pay trading fees, or for trading \u8212\'20\'14 just like Bitcoin and others.\par \par \uc2 Blockchain: A type of distributed ledger, written on open source software. It is a growing database of time-stamped transactions that cannot be altered. Each new transaction is verified by a network of computers and added as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblock\u8221\'20\'1D to the chain.\par \par \uc2 Burning coins: Inflation is one of the enemies of cryptocurrencies. Thus, there is a counterpart to minting new coins: burning them, thereby removing them from circulation. For stablecoins, burning is particularly important to keep the token supply equal to the asset backing they have.\par \par \uc2 Cardano: A blockchain network that can facilitate peer-to-peer transactions with its own digital currency, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The name honours English mathematician and writer \b \highlight22\uc2 Ada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Lovelace, who is viewed as the world\u8217\'20\'19s first software engineer because she created an algorithm in the 19th century. It promises to use less energy than Bitcoin or ethereum because it uses proof-of-stake protocols to verify transactions. It was developed by \uc2 Charles Hoskinson\uc2 , a co-founder of ethereum, who left after a dispute with other fellow co-founders, including \uc2 Vitalik Buterin\uc2 . Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 Ada\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the fastest growing cryptocurrencies, with more people holding it on trading platform \uc2 eToro\uc2  than Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Central bank digital currencies (CBDCs): Proposed digital currencies run by central banks, rather than created by private companies. They would use the same technology but would be backed by reserves. Central bankers have been spurred on by fears that efforts such as \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposed cryptocurrency could impact monetary policy, and destabilise financial markets or cross-border money transfers.\par \par \uc2 Coin: A cryptocurrency that lives on its own independent blockchain. Examples include Bitcoin and ethereum. Distinct from a token.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 : The largest US-listed exchange for buyers and sellers of cryptocurrencies and tokens. It also allows customers to deposit their crypto assets and lend them out, earning interest far in excess of prevailing bank rates. In 2023, the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  sued the San Francisco-based company, arguing it had been violating US securities law for at least four years, by failing to register as a broker, national securities exchange or clearing agency. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has said it will fight the suit.\par \par \uc2 Cold storage: Storing crypto assets on a computer in a vault, which is not connected to the internet. Many cold storage wallets do not accept as many kinds of cryptocurrencies and are more expensive storage options. Consequently, many traders prefer to use a hot wallet.\par \par \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  (CFTC)\par \par \uc2 The main US regulator for derivatives. The agency has determined that, in legal terms, virtual currencies like Bitcoin are commodities. That means it has jurisdiction to oversee derivatives that use a digital currency and potentially hand out penalties if there is fraud or manipulation of those derivatives.\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency: A currency created digitally, usually by private companies, and named after the cryptographic maths that make it possible. It was conceived in the depths of the financial crisis by \uc2 Satoshi Nakamoto\uc2  as a way for people to make electronic payments without going through any financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchange: A venue for buying and selling cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin and ethereum. They often also offer loans and custody of assets, and other services that a traditional exchange cannot. Examples of crypto exchanges include \uc2 Binance\uc2 , \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , \uc2 Huobi\uc2 , Bybit, Kraken, \uc2 Gemini\uc2 , \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  and \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Crypto mixing- A type of money transfer designed to obscure the audit trails that would normally be available to the public on the digital ledgers that track cryptocurrency moves. In a mixing service customers can deposit tokens such as bitcoin using one wallet address. The funds are then mixed into a single pool containing all users\u8217\'20\'19 funds. When it is drawn out it has a different address, making the owner untraceable. Unsurprisingly, the US thinks such services are ideal vehicles for illicit activity like sanctions busting, money laundering and supporting North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear programme.\par \par \uc2 DApp: A computer application that runs on a decentralised finance network, such as a distributed ledger.\par \par \uc2 DAO (decentralised autonomous organisation): An organisation whose rules are automated or developed by consensus among the members. It is designed to work unlike a typical corporate structure, where power lies in the hands of an executive or board.\par \par \uc2 Decentralised finance (DeFi): An umbrella term for a collection of cryptoasset projects that aim to do away with a centralised intermediary \u8212\'20\'14 like a bank or an exchange \u8212\'20\'14 to provide financial services. They use DApps to execute common services like lending, savings accounts and trading coins.\par \par \uc2 Decentralised trading protocol: Sometimes referred to as a decentralised exchange, or DEX. It is a network that allows users to buy and sell digital assets directly with each other, bypassing intermediaries that might impose fees, such as an exchange or clearing house. Automated market makers use smart contracts which can trade 24 hours a day, seven days a week. Older trading networks, such as Uniswap and SushiSwap, are written on ethereum but newer networks may use alternative protocols like Solana or Polkadot. However, some networks may suffer from low liquidity. There is also little recourse for users who find their security hacked and assets stolen.\par \par \uc2 Diem: The yet-to-be launched digital coin by \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and previously known as Libra. It has been credited with jolting central banks and regulators into realising that private cryptocurrency initiatives were becoming too big to ignore, and to start on their own CBDCs. The intense scrutiny led \uc2 Facebook\uc2  to change the name from Libra and scale back its ambitions in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Digital Currency Group: Venture capital firm which has funded dozens of coins and companies in the digital assets industry, including exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and broker \uc2 eToro\uc2 . It owns investment firm Grayscale, trade news site CoinDesk, and is also parent to the crypto-lending unit Genesis, which filed for US bankruptcy protection in early 2023, and left creditors short on at least $3.4bn, after it was toppled in the industry-wide turmoil following the collapse of the FTX exchange.\par \par \uc2 Distributed ledger: A public register of deals shared and replicated by a network of computers. They work together to verify transactions and create an immutable ledger, and do away with the need for a central authority. It is similar to a blockchain but it does not need to have its data structured in blocks. Nor does it need to use proof of work to mine tokens.\par \par \uc2 dogecoin: An alt-coin that purposely began as a joke, to highlight the speculative nature of cryptocurrencies in 2013. It uses a Japanese Shiba Inu dog as its mascot and has surged in popularity and value despite its beginnings.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum: The world\u8217\'20\'19s second most actively-traded cryptocurrency and the token associated with the ethereum blockchain.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum: A developer-run blockchain technology co-founded by \uc2 Vitalik Buterin\uc2 , a Canadian-Russian computer science student. Its aim is to make blockchains more useful and revolutionary than simply to serve as a database for transactions. Its technology can hold assets, enables programmers to code functions for buying and selling into smart contracts, and is typically also the building block for most DApps for finance.\par \par \uc2 Fiat\uc2  currency: A traditional currency backed and regulated by a central bank \u8212\'20\'14 such as the US dollar, euro, sterling and yen.\par \par \uc2 Flippening: A term the moment when ethereum overtakes Bitcoin as the biggest and most valuable cryptocurrency.\par \par \uc2 Fork: Developers sometimes disagree on how a blockchain should be run and, if they cannot settle their differences, the ultimate step is to create a fork in the network. One side will use newer software and the existing network will rely on the older version. It means that two incompatible versions of the blockchain emerge, based on different principles and with different user bases. Forks can take place for a number of reasons including concerns over outdated and insecure software, or a need to reverse the log of transactions following a hack, or a need to return investors\u8217\'20\'19 funds to them.\par \par \uc2 FTX\uc2 : The now bankrupt company was one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest and most high-profile cryptocurrency exchanges in its heyday. Founded in 2019, it rose to prominence by enabling investors to trade various digital coins and exchange them for traditional currencies. But it fell into financial difficulty and collapsed. Once valued at $32bn, \uc2 FTX\uc2  filed for bankruptcy in 2022, leaving customers short on as much as $8bn of its liabilities. Weeks later US regulators charged the company and several of its senior management with misusing client funds, wire fraud and conspiracy to commit money laundering. The relationship with its associated trading firm \uc2 Alameda Research\uc2 , at the time almost entirely owned by co-\uc2 FTX\uc2  founder and then-CEO \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , also came under scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 FUD: An acronym for \u8220\'20\'1Cfear, uncertainty and doubt\u8221\'20\'1D, used as a dismissive label for negative information about cryptocurrencies \u8212\'20\'14 and normally to imply that criticisms of digital assets are invalid or misleading. The Fud label is often applied to critiques focusing on Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s environmental impact or the use of cryptocurrencies for money laundering. People who spread Fud are called Fudsters.\par \par \uc2 Funding rate: A measure of the direction of traders\u8217\'20\'19 collective positions in crypto. It works in tandem with a perpetual futures contract. The funding rate is designed to bring the price of the futures contract closer to the index it tracks. The rate is based on the difference between the spot market and the futures price. It is expressed as a percentage. If it is above zero, it is described as positive as it shows there is more demand for long futures contracts. If it is below zero, it is described as negative. To balance the positions, traders betting in one direction pay traders who have taken the opposing position. If the funding rate is positive, traders who are long of a token price have to pay those who are short. If sentiment is negative, traders with a short position pay those who have gone long. The payments in either direction continue during a set window, often every eight hours, until the price of the future converges with that of the index again. The payments are based on the notional size of a trader\u8217\'20\'19s position \u8212\'20\'14 meaning they can be substantial for highly leveraged bets.\par \par \uc2 Gas Fees: The fees paid by users to compensate for the amount of computing energy needed to verify a transaction on the ethereum network. They are intended to prevent nefarious actors from spamming the network. Prices can rise and fall depending on demand. Users have complained about ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s fees, which can cost anything from $20 \u8212\'20\'14 $100, because ethereum is so heavily used.\par \par \uc2 Gemini\uc2 : An exchange for buyers and sellers of cryptocurrencies and tokens set up in 2014 by the Winklevoss twins. Customers can also deposit assets and earn interest far in excess of prevailing bank rates.\par \par \uc2 Governance tokens: Tokens that give holders voting powers on a blockchain protocol. They are mainly used in DeFi projects so systems can remain decentralised and no one party makes the decisions on the project\u8217\'20\'19s future direction.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Investment Trust: A fund that operates the world\u8217\'20\'19s most popular Bitcoin exchange-traded fund.\par \par \uc2 Have fun staying poor: The ultimate retort from crypto enthusiasts to sceptics \u8212\'20\'14 expressing their pity for non-believers. It is usually used to counter criticism of Bitcoin or other digital assets and it implies that sceptics do not understand the full implications of blockchain technology.\par \par \uc2 Hodl: The battle cry of the long-term cryptocurrency holder. Originally a humorous misspelling of \u8216\'20\'18hold\u8217\'20\'19 found on a cryptocurrency forum in 2013 and sometimes thought to be an acronym for \u8220\'20\'1CHolding On For Dear Life\u8221\'20\'1D, the frantic tone associated with its use has struck a chord with the wider crypto community. Hodling is not simply about keeping crypto-investments no matter how low they fall. It also reflects an almost religious belief in the inevitability of a return to profitability and a rejection of both the fickle, unmanly day trader and the myopic, untrustworthy crypto-sceptic.\par \par \uc2 Hot wallet: A virtual wallet to store crypto assets. It is kept online which means it is easier to access and enables users to trade more quickly. But being online makes it more susceptible to being hacked, so some people prefer to keep their assets in cold storage.\par \par \uc2 ICO: Like an initial public offering, an initial coin offering is a tool for fundraising. But the similarities end there. Investors get some of the new currency, as opposed to stock in the company. And, unlike IPOs, ICOs lack any investor protection: they can be set up with just a website, a utopian mission statement and some ad spend. After a surge in popularity in 2017-18, ICOs came under sustained scrutiny from regulators in the US, UK and Europe over the dangers they posed to consumers. In 2019, messaging apps Kik and Telegram were both sued over their ICOs by the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Laser eyes: A social media meme in which users change or edit their profile pictures to make their eyes look like they emit red laser beams. It denotes a fan of cryptocurrencies, with the light-emitting powers variously interpreted to mean a user has special powers of sight and an iron will to make Bitcoin an instrument of economic empowerment.\par \par \uc2 Layer 2: A secondary network or technology run by a third party and built on top of an existing blockchain to improve its efficiency. For example, some blockchains like Bitcoin and ethereum cannot handle vast quantities of trades at high speed, affecting the users of some DApps. A layer 2 network can handle the bulk of the transaction processing legwork, so the original blockchain can scale.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity pool: A central feature of decentralised trading. Customers do not trade on an order book but against other participants in the pool, who have also filled up the pool with funds that sit on smart contracts.\par \par \uc2 Maximalist: A crypto-purist who believes with unwavering conviction that their preferred coin, be it Bitcoin or Ethereum, is the only one that has value.\u160\'00\'A0\par \par \uc2 Memecoin: A cryptocurrency that is associated with a meme or viral online joke. dogecoin is a popular example of a memecoin.\par \par \uc2 Metaverse: A vision of the future internet. An immersive virtual reality world where people will be able to pursue all aspects of life as if in a parallel digital universe.\par \par \uc2 Mining: The act of employing a large network of computers to work together to solve cryptographic calculations that verify cryptocurrency transactions. Typically, one party will solve the puzzle, known as a hash, that creates the next block in the chain. The others will verify it. In return for maintaining the blockchain, miners are rewarded with new tokens for being the first to solve the cryptographic proof. They also collect transaction fees.\par \par \uc2 Mooning, aka Going to the Moon: When the price and trading volume of a cryptocurrency are both soaring.\par \par \uc2 Musk, Elon: One of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most influential cryptocurrency advocates, with the power to raise or drop prices of coins with a single tweet or Saturday evening TV appearance. Sometimes sells electric cars, too.\par \par \uc2 Nakamoto, Satoshi: The pseudonymous creator \u8212\'20\'14 or creators \u8212\'20\'14 of Bitcoin. The seminal moment was the publication of a whitepaper in 2008, weeks after \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  collapsed amid the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 NFT: A non-fungible token. A unit of information stored as a token on a blockchain, usually an ethereum blockchain. However, it is not fungible \u8212\'20\'14 meaning it cannot be interchanged with another token. That makes the token unique and turns its blockchain into a digital form of provenance. It can only have one owner. Some artists and sellers of collectible memorabilia have begun experimenting with selling NFTs. But owning the token only proves that someone has ownership of the \u8220\'20\'1Coriginal\u8221\'20\'1D work, and does not necessarily include its copyright or its intellectual property rights.\par \par \uc2 NGMI: \u8220\'20\'1CNot Going To Make It\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 slang for missing out on the profits of a trade. Its opposite is \u8220\'20\'1CGMI\u8221\'20\'1D, or Going to Make It.\par \par \uc2 Nocoiner: A sceptic who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t own any cryptocurrency, believes it has little to no value and suspects it might be a Ponzi scheme that will fail.\par \par \uc2 Node: Its definition varies, but is usually understood to mean a physical point on a computer network where an activity takes place. Sometimes, it can be to collect and distribute information; sometimes, it is where transactions on a blockchain are verified.\par \par \uc2 OpenSea: The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest peer-to-peer marketplace for trading NFTs.\par \par \uc2 Oracle\uc2 : A third party that acts as a bridge between traditional markets and the crypto world. It gathers data from the outside world, such as asset prices, and sends it to a blockchain or distributed ledger. That data can be used in smart contracts for other crypto trading projects. It can also work in reverse, using information in smart contracts in the outside world.\par \par \uc2 PancakeSwap: A decentralised trading protocol based on the Binance blockchain. Customers can exchange \uc2 Binance\uc2  tokens. It uses automated market makers to trade assets.\par \par \uc2 Pig butchering: Drawing an unflattering analogy to fattening farm pigs before slaughter, the term refers to a type of cryptocurrency scam that involves befriending or entering into a romantic relationship with the unwitting victim, to gain trust before convincing them to make a sketchy investment.\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  futures: Type of futures contract more commonly used in crypto than in conventional markets. The expiration date on a traditional future that tracks the price of oil, gas or stock indices helps link the future to the price of the underlying asset, since the holder typically takes delivery of the asset on that date. \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  futures can be held indefinitely as the funding rate mechanism links the futures price with the spot price. Derivatives markets usually have more volume than spot markets, so often provide signals into sentiment and likely short-term moves in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Private key: The complex password needed to access a virtual currency wallet.\par \par \uc2 Proof-of-stake: A system for mining cryptocurrencies that requires users to stake their coins as collateral to become a verifier on the network. It is largely associated with the ethereum blockchain. Unlike proof-of-work systems, verifiers are chosen at random to create blocks and validate proposed blocks. If they attest to fraudulent blocks, they will lose their staked coins. As no coins are mined, the process should not require vast amounts of computing energy. However, it has been hard to scale and ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s blockchain has struggled to keep up with demand. Critics have argued the system favours richer participants because the more coins a miner owns, the more mining power it has.\par \par \uc2 Proof-of-work Used in mining, it allows one party to prove it has solved the cryptographic puzzle to validate a transaction, while the others verify the work. Its aim is to prevent the same coins being spent twice with two different parties. Largely associated with the Bitcoin blockchain, it has been criticised for its high energy consumption and slow speed. Developers are looking at proof-of-stake mining as a cheaper, faster and less environmentally-damaging alternative.\par \par \uc2 Pyth: A DeFi project and \uc2 Oracle\uc2 , built by some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest high-speed traders as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpotential game changer\u8221\'20\'1D for trading stocks and other assets on blockchain technology.\par \par \uc2 Rekt In the world of gaming, you might shout rekt when you gun down an opponent in Fortnite, the violent and popular video game. In cryptocurrencies, someone is rekt if they suffer a loss as a result of a bad crypto investment. A cryptocurrency that has gone down significantly in value could also be said to be rekt.\par \par \uc2 Rugpull A common method of defrauding investors in the wild west world of DeFi, where anyone can list a coin and compete for investors\u8217\'20\'19 money. Scammers set-up a new coin that promises to be the next big moneymaking opportunity. After attracting investors, usually via chat rooms or other social media channels, and convincing enough of them to put money into the projects, the developers of the coin then vanish into thin (decentralised) air.\par \par \uc2 Security token: Similar to the securities that are traded on a stock or bond market but ownership is recorded on a blockchain rather than in a central depository. The tokens often promise a share in future profits or repayments. Regulators around the world usually regard them as in their regulatory jurisdiction.\par \par \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 : The US securities regulator. Its jurisdiction over crypto markets is limited but does regulate digital assets securities. The SEC chair, \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2 , has called on legislators to give it the power to regulate crypto exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Sharding: Splitting a network into separate but linked ledgers, so it can reduce the strain on each node in the network by no longer requiring it to validate every transaction.\par \par \uc2 Saylor, Michael: Chief executive of \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 , a software company that has taken the unusual step of buying thousands of Bitcoins. In 2020, he tweeted that Bitcoin was \u8220\'20\'1Ca swarm of cyber hornets serving the goddess of wisdom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Silbert, Barry: Entrepreneur, early investor in the crypto industry, and founder of \uc2 Digital Currency Group\uc2 . A Bitcoin whale.\par \par \uc2 Smart contract: A computer program that can contain financial assets and be coded with the ability to execute actions by itself, if certain conditions are met. That could include transferring funds or sending notifications. Smart contracts play a crucial role in decentralised trading protocols.\par \par \uc2 Stablecoins: Cryptocurrencies pegged to other assets, usually the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest and most stable currencies. They act as crypto-native dollars and a bridge between crypto and traditional financial worlds. They also allow traders to more easily convert traditional currencies into cryptocurrencies for trading. The coins can be lent as collateral for trading, or to generate high yields in the form of interest. They are supposed to have a fixed price and be backed by reserves at all times, allowing users to redeem them. However, critics have questioned where some stablecoins keep their reserves and whether the assets can be quickly recovered and redeemed. The two biggest stablecoin operators are Tether and USDC, run by Circle. A few stablecoins are backed by other cryptocurrencies or baskets of other cryptocurrencies. They use algorithms to buy and sell in order to keep themselves fully backed. But these algorithmic stablecoins can collapse if anything happens to the cryptocurrencies to which they are pegged. They remain a small part of the market.\par \par \uc2 Solana: A blockchain protocol that can handle smart contracts and claims faster speeds and lower transaction costs than ethereum.\par \par \uc2 Staking: A protocol that aims to boost asset owners\u8217\'20\'19 earnings. Users lock their crypto in their wallet but give permission for a third party, often an exchange, to stake their crypto on DeFi projects that offer interest or yield farming. The barriers to staking are quite high and users normally need to hold a lot of a particular cryptocurrency first. \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  both offer staking.\par \par \uc2 Tether: The largest and most controversial stablecoin, with over 60bn tokens in circulation. It is nominally pegged to the US dollar and says all its tokens are backed by dollars, one-for-one. It plays an important role in the cryptocurrency ecosystem, because its tokens are used by investors who want to leverage their returns on more volatile cryptocurrencies. However, the New York attorney-general ruled it had deceived clients over its reserves after it suffered a serious loss of funds when its payment processors\u8217\'20\'19 accounts were frozen. Tether did not admit to any wrongdoing, but paid a settlement of $18.5mn Its self-declared commercial paper (a form of debt security) holdings would make it one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest investors in the market, according to \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Token: A unit built on an existing blockchain and intended to be an incentive or reward for developing other projects on that blockchain. The best known example is ERC20, a token on the ethereum blockchain, which has built other digital assets and currencies. Distinct from a coin.\par \par \uc2 Trustless: A central tenet of the crypto industry. Computing systems like blockchain eliminate the need for a trusted third party, like a bank or clearing house, to check or execute transactions.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap: A decentralised trading protocol built on the ethereum blockchain. It is also the name of the company set up by Hayden Adams, the developer behind Uniswap.\par \par \uc2 Whale: Much like their marine counterparts, cryptocurrency whales are reclusive creatures whose activity has an effect on the whole ecosystem. They are individuals or institutions that hold a large proportion of the coins of a particular cryptocurrency. A rule of thumb is that a whale owns more than 5 per cent of a given coin. That makes them key actors in the price of the asset. Holding the asset can keep it out of circulation, boosting its price. Selling can cause the price to dip, especially if the volume floods the market. In an unregulated market, it invites accusations they are manipulating the market. Few whales are known because identities are anonymous, but they can be recognised by the internet addresses controlled by a single network participant. Known bitcoin whales include the Winklevoss twins.\par \par \uc2 Whitepaper: Part marketing tool, part technical documentation and part vision statement, a whitepaper sets out how a cryptocurrency works, what it is trying to do and the creator\u8217\'20\'19s projections for profitability. Whitepapers have often been associated with the ICO craze. However, whitepapers are produced by almost all cryptocurrency companies as standard procedure. The most famous was written by \uc2 Satoshi Nakamoto\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Winklevoss, Cameron and Tyler: Twin brothers who were early and vocal backers of Bitcoin when it was still a hobby for enthusiasts in the early 2010s. Regarded as Bitcoin whales because they bought large holdings when the currency was worth only cents. They rose to pre-crypto fame because of their claims that \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  stole the idea for \uc2 Facebook\uc2  from them.\par \par \uc2 Wrapped token: A cryptocurrency token pegged to the value of another token. They have identical values but enable one token to lives on a Blockchain that it was not issued on. For example, Bitcoin and ethereum blockchains cannot talk to each other; but a wrapped token acts as a bridge between the two.\par \par \uc2 Yield farming: The practice of looking through the DeFi world for best yields available from more obscure projects and coins. These opportunities can advertise interest rates as high as several thousand per cent to pull in digital cash but can also be short lived.\par \par \uc2 Additional reporting by Joshua Oliver, Eva Szalay and Siddharth Venkataramakrishnan, Daria Mosolova and Camilla Bell-Davies\par \par \uc2 Document FTCOM00020211021ehal0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin gains $2K in hours after BTC price bounces near previous all-time high\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 396 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nothing can keep Bitcoin down as BTC price action returns above $66,000.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) passed $66,000 again on Oct. 21 after fresh macro turbulence sparked a retest of previous all-time highs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/59bae720-1cea-4be6-aeed-70ac73becd50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Evergrande fails to hold Bitcoin bulls back\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BITSTAMP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD recovering from a dip to $64,000 overnight.\par \par \uc2 The move had come in step with a comedown in stocks, which were reacting to renewed concerns over Chinese property giant Evergrande.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, Bitcoin managed to preserve higher levels, resulting in only a brief trip below the $64,900 threshold, which had held as the BTC record since April this year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  successfully retested the orange area as support to reach a new All Time High\par \par \uc2 Now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  is dipping to turn its previous old All Time High into support (blue){\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qJZnm8X387"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qJZnm8X387}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1451108461429903360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMarkets always go higher than the majority expects. Probably what will happen in coming months,\u8221\'20\'1D a still \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1451092137400020994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summarized}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers.\par \par \uc2 $75,000 next target\par \par \uc2 Wednesday, Oct. 20, saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-bitcoin-officially-hits-new-all-time-high-above-65k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new all-time highs}}}\uc2  of over $67,000 after a squeeze took BTC/USD $3,000 higher.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-10-20-btc-eth-bnb-ada-xrp-sol-dot-doge-luna-uni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 10/20: BTC, ETH, BNB, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI}}}\par \par \uc2 The monthly candle for October, analysts noted, is already larger than the entire Bitcoin all-time high from December 2017.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBTC is testing its old ATH for support,\u8221\'20\'1D Dutch crypto consultancy and education platform Eight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eight_global/status/1451085866525417475/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in its latest update on the day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we bounce from here some levels to keep an eye on are around 75k, 87k, and 96k, derived from recent price action using the Fibonacci retracement tool.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1339b78c-66c3-4300-9252-44d77712335b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD chart with Fibonacci levels. Source: Eight/\uc2 Twitter\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/200k-btc-price-programmed-as-bitcoin-heads-toward-2nd-rsi-peak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , Fibonacci is responsible for long-term BTC price findings, which currently put the peak of this cycle\u8217\'20\'19s bull run at as much as $300,000. The trough, by contrast, could be anywhere from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/think-60k-is-the-top-this-bitcoin-fractal-suggests-it-s-the-next-bear-market-bottom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $47,000 to $60,000}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 still an order of magnitude higher than last cycle\u8217\'20\'19s $3,100 floor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvNDJhMWFkNjAtMjE0Zi00OTA5LTk4ZTktOGRiM2U2NDBmZWRmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211021ehal0005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin gains $2K in hours after BTC price bounces near previous all-time high\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 394 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nothing can keep Bitcoin down as BTC price action returns above $66,000.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) passed $66,000 again on Oct. 21 after a fresh macro turbulence sparked a retest of previous all-time highs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/59bae720-1cea-4be6-aeed-70ac73becd50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Evergrande fails to hold Bitcoin bulls back\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BITSTAMP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD recovering from a dip to $64,000 overnight.\par \par \uc2 The move had come in step with a comedown in stocks, which were reacting to renewed concerns over Chinese property giant Evergrande.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, Bitcoin managed to preserve higher levels, resulting only a brief trip below the $64,900 threshold which had held as the BTC record since April this year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  successfully retested the orange area as support to reach a new All Time High\par \par \uc2 Now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  is dipping to turn its previous old All Time High into support (blue){\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qJZnm8X387"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qJZnm8X387}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1451108461429903360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 "Markets always go higher than the majority expects. Probably what will happen in coming months," a still \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1451092137400020994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summarized}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers.\par \par \uc2 $75,000 next target\par \par \uc2 Wednesday saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-bitcoin-officially-hits-new-all-time-high-above-65k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new all-time highs}}}\uc2  of over $67,000 after a squeeze took BTC/USD $3,000 higher.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-10-20-btc-eth-bnb-ada-xrp-sol-dot-doge-luna-uni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 10/20: BTC, ETH, BNB, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI}}}\par \par \uc2 The monthly candle for October, analysts noted, is already larger than the entire Bitcoin all-time high from December 2017.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBTC is testing its old ATH for support,\u8221\'20\'1D Dutch crypto consultancy and education platform Eight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eight_global/status/1451085866525417475/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in its latest update on the day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we bounce from here some levels to keep an eye on are around 75k, 87k, and 96k, derived from recent price action using the Fibonacci retracement tool.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1339b78c-66c3-4300-9252-44d77712335b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD chart with Fibonacci levels. Source: Eight/ Twitter\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/200k-btc-price-programmed-as-bitcoin-heads-toward-2nd-rsi-peak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , Fibonacci is responsible for long-term BTC price findings which currently put the peak of this cycle\u8217\'20\'19s bull run at as much as $300,000. The trough, by contrast, could be anywhere from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/think-60k-is-the-top-this-bitcoin-fractal-suggests-it-s-the-next-bear-market-bottom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $47,000 to $60,000}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 still an order of magnitude higher than last cycle\u8217\'20\'19s $3,100 floor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvNDJhMWFkNjAtMjE0Zi00OTA5LTk4ZTktOGRiM2U2NDBmZWRmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211021ehal0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/20: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,786 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s breakout to $67,000 also sent the total crypto market capitalization to a new all-time high and is a signal that altcoins could soon embark on a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-bitcoin-officially-hits-new-all-time-high-above-65k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged to a new all-time high}}}\uc2  on Oct. 20, hitting close to $67,000. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-nears-its-own-all-time-high-as-eth-price-retakes-4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke above its immediate resistance}}}\uc2  and has started its march toward the all-time high. This pushed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-market-cap-hits-new-all-time-high-as-btc-eth-soar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total market capitalization of the crypto sector}}}\uc2  to a new all-time high above $2.64 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The successful debut of the ProShares\u8217\'20\'19 Bitcoin Strategy exchange-traded fund (BITO) acted as the trigger to boost sentiment in the crypto space. The ProShares\u8217\'20\'19 ETF trading volume on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-futures-etf-debuts-with-highest-ever-first-day-natural-volume-of-1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first day of the launch exceeded $1 billion}}}\uc2 , making it the second-most successful ETF debut based on the trading volume on day one.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/245f493c-2510-45eb-8794-27ce7272190b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 A panel of 50 fintech industry specialists, commissioned by Finder, believes that strong on-chain fundamentals, a favorable macro environment and approval of the \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  could send Bitcoin to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fintech-panel-forecasts-80k-btc-price-top-this-year-finder-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $80,000 by the end of the year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin piggyback on the positive sentiment created due to the successful launch of the \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  and continue its northward march? Will altcoins also resume their up-move? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke above the immediate resistance at $62,933 on Oct. 19 and that was followed by another sharp up-move on Oct. 20, thrusting the price above the previous all-time high at $64,854 made on April 14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e05f1a02-3e94-4ff4-86f6-9a21a1367e4a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain the price above the breakout level at $64,854, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up further. The BTC/USDT pair could then rally to the overhead resistance at $75,000.\par \par \uc2 The sharp up-move of the past few days has pushed the relative strength index (RSI) above 78, suggesting that the rally may be overextended in the short term. This could result in a few days of consolidation or a minor correction.\par \par \uc2 If bulls do not give up much ground from the current level, it will suggest strength and improve the prospects of the continuation of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The critical level to watch on the downside is $60,000. A break and close below this support will be the first sign that traders are aggressively booking profits at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether bounced off the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern on Oct. 19, suggesting that bulls are buying on dips to this support. Strong buying has pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $4,027.88 on Oct. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e2bc3208-534c-4d8d-8dc2-f6cb237a27eb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory indicate advantage to the bulls. If buyers sustain the price above $4,027.88, the ETH/USDT pair could rally to the all-time high at $4,372.72.\par \par \uc2 This level may again act as a stiff resistance but if bulls clear the hurdle, the pair could reach the pattern target at $4,657 and then challenge the psychological level at $5,000.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $3,200.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is gradually moving higher toward $518.90, which had acted as a tough barrier on two previous occasions. Hence, the bears may again try to defend this level with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/536cce72-c190-44e5-a80b-ffbebe7f7c7b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $518.90, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($450). A strong rebound off this level will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying the dips.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the likelihood of a break and close above $518.90. The pair could then start its northward march to the pattern target at $554. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate if the price turns down and breaks below the right shoulder at $392.20.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is attempting to bounce off the support line of the symmetrical triangle pattern. If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA ($2.19), the altcoin could rally to the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5ffb9fae-8bba-4042-ab86-a98f6fc0d9ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the triangle will signal that the uncertainty has resolved in favor of the buyers. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rally to $2.47 and if this level is crossed, the up-move could reach $2.80.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the triangle, it will suggest that supply exceeds demand. The pair could then decline to the critical support at $1.87.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) formed an inside-day candlestick pattern on Oct. 18 and 19, suggesting indecision among the bulls and the bears. This uncertainty resolved to the upside on Oct. 20, with a break above $1.10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/63eca016-ac77-4ad3-9f2f-3fb860e6f47d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to push the price above the downtrend line. If they manage to do that, the XRP/USDT pair could rise to $1.24 and if this resistance is crossed, the next stop could be the critical level at $1.41.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the downtrend line, the pair could again drop to $1. A break and close below this support will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  descending triangle pattern that could result in a decline to $0.85.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully defended the moving averages in the past few days, indicating accumulation at lower levels. The buyers will now try to push Solana (SOL) above the overhead resistance zone between $171.47 and $177.79.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/3215dce1-53ec-4107-be76-821a8ab19b81.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A close above $177.79 will complete an ascending triangle pattern, which has a target objective at $226.94. The rally may not be linear as bears are expected to pose a stiff challenge at the psychological level at $200 and then at the all-time high at $216.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the current level, it will suggest that bears are selling aggressively on rallies. A break and close below the trendline will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The SOL/USDT pair could then drop to the critical support at $116.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully held Polkadot (DOT) above the breakout level at $38.77 for the past few days. This suggests strong accumulation by the bulls as they anticipate the rally to resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/6f64933f-f023-4694-a810-b579b68bbb5b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI just below the overbought territory indicate that buyers have the upper hand. A break and close above $44.78 could push the price to the all-time high at $49.78.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($37.84), it will suggest that bears have made a strong comeback. The DOT/USDT pair could then drop to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($33.63).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cointelegraph-consulting-etfs-listed-what-s-next-for-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Consulting: ETFs listed \u8212\'20\'14 What\u8217\'20\'19s next for Bitcoin?}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line on Oct. 18 but could not sustain the higher levels as seen from the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The buyers again tried to clear the overhead hurdle at the downtrend line on Oct. 19 but failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/07d169a0-5e84-49c6-969b-2e26f356f65c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 After twice being unsuccessful, the bulls are again trying to drive and sustain the price above the downtrend line on Oct. 20. Such a move will invalidate the developing descending triangle pattern, clearing the path for a possible rally to $0.32 and then $0.35.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the downtrend line and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($0.23), it will suggest that bears are defending the downtrend line aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the strong support zone at $0.21 to $0.19.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token broke below the 50-day SMA ($36.66) on Oct. 17 but the bears could not pull the price below the strong support at $34.86. The failure to do so seems to have attracted buying from aggressive bulls who have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $39.75 on Oct. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/ec57d2a8-b977-4de4-8168-d586424589ad.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LUNA/USDT pair could now rise to $45.01 where the bears are likely to offer a stiff resistance. If the price turns down from this level but rebounds off the breakout level at $39.75, it will suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above $45.01 could push the pair to the all-time high at $49.54. On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $39.75, it will signal strong selling at higher levels. The pair could then drop to $34.86.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) has been trading in a tight range between the neckline of the possible inverse H&S and the 20-day EMA ($25.32). This indicates indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5289e5dc-2cf0-48f9-b3bc-c247595b6b05.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the neckline will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The UNI/USDT pair could then rally to $31.41 and if this level is crossed, the up-move may reach the pattern target at $36.98.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level and plummets below the moving averages, the decline may extend to $22. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break below it could sink the pair to $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvMDUzMzk1MzctYTQyNS00YTk1LTkwYzMtOWI5YjRiZDE1NjhiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211021ehak0008p\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/20: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,767 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s breakout to $67,000 also sent the total crypto market capitalization to a new all-time high and is a signal that altcoins could soon embark on a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-bitcoin-officially-hits-new-all-time-high-above-65k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged to a new all-time high today}}}\uc2 , hitting close to $67,000. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-nears-its-own-all-time-high-as-eth-price-retakes-4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke above its immediate resistance}}}\uc2  and has started its march toward the all-time high. This pushed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-market-cap-hits-new-all-time-high-as-btc-eth-soar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total market capitalization of the crypto sector}}}\uc2  to a new all-time high above $2.64 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The successful debut of the ProShares\u8217\'20\'19 Bitcoin Strategy exchange-traded fund (BITO) acted as the trigger to boost sentiment in the crypto space. The ProShares\u8217\'20\'19 ETF trading volume on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-futures-etf-debuts-with-highest-ever-first-day-natural-volume-of-1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first day of the launch exceeded $1 billion}}}\uc2 , making it the second-most successful ETF debut based on the trading volume on day one.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/245f493c-2510-45eb-8794-27ce7272190b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 A panel of 50 fintech industry specialists, commissioned by Finder, believes that strong on-chain fundamentals, a favorable macro environment, and approval of the \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  could send Bitcoin to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fintech-panel-forecasts-80k-btc-price-top-this-year-finder-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $80,000 by the end of the year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin piggyback on the positive sentiment created due to the successful launch of the \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  and continue its northward march? Will altcoins also resume their up-move? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke above the immediate resistance at $62,933 on Oct. 19 and that was followed by another sharp up-move today, thrusting the price above the previous all-time high at $64,854 made on April 14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e05f1a02-3e94-4ff4-86f6-9a21a1367e4a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain the price above the breakout level at $64,854, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up further. The BTC/USDT pair could then rally to the overhead resistance at $75,000.\par \par \uc2 The sharp up-move of the past few days has pushed the relative strength index (RSI) above 78, suggesting that the rally may be overextended in the short term. This could result in a few days of consolidation or a minor correction.\par \par \uc2 If bulls do not give up much ground from the current level, it will suggest strength and improve the prospects of the continuation of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The critical level to watch on the downside is $60,000. A break and close below this support will be the first sign that traders are aggressively booking profits at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether bounced off the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern on Oct. 19, suggesting that bulls are buying on dips to this support. Strong buying has pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $4,027.88 today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e2bc3208-534c-4d8d-8dc2-f6cb237a27eb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory indicate advantage to the bulls. If buyers sustain the price above $4,027.88, the ETH/USDT pair could rally to the all-time high at $4,372.72.\par \par \uc2 This level may again act as a stiff resistance but if bulls clear the hurdle, the pair could reach the pattern target at $4,657 and then challenge the psychological level at $5,000.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $3,200.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is gradually moving higher toward $518.90, which had acted as a tough barrier on two previous occasions. Hence, the bears may again try to defend this level with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/536cce72-c190-44e5-a80b-ffbebe7f7c7b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $518.90, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($450). A strong rebound off this level will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying the dips.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the likelihood of a break and close above $518.90. The pair could then start its northward march to the pattern target at $554. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate if the price turns down and breaks below the right shoulder at $392.20.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is attempting to bounce off the support line of the symmetrical triangle pattern. If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA ($2.19) the altcoin could rally to the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5ffb9fae-8bba-4042-ab86-a98f6fc0d9ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the triangle will signal that the uncertainty has resolved in favor of the buyers. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rally to $2.47 and if this level is crossed, the up-move could reach $2.80.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the triangle, it will suggest that supply exceeds demand. The pair could then decline to the critical support at $1.87.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  formed an inside-day candlestick pattern on Oct. 18 and 19, suggesting indecision among the bulls and the bears. This uncertainty resolved to the upside today with a break above $1.10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/63eca016-ac77-4ad3-9f2f-3fb860e6f47d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to push the price above the downtrend line. If they manage to do that, the XRP/USDT pair could rise to $1.24 and if this resistance is crossed, the next stop could be the critical level at $1.41.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the downtrend line, the pair could again drop to $1. A break and close below this support will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  descending triangle pattern that could result in a decline to $0.85.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully defended the moving averages in the past few days, indicating accumulation at lower levels. The buyers will now try to push Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance zone between $171.47 and $177.79.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/3215dce1-53ec-4107-be76-821a8ab19b81.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A close above $177.79 will complete an ascending triangle pattern, which has a target objective at $226.94. The rally may not be linear as bears are expected to pose a stiff challenge at the psychological level at $200 and then at the all-time high at $216.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the current level, it will suggest that bears are aggressively selling on rallies. A break and close below the trendline will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The SOL/USDT pair could then drop to the critical support at $116.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully held Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above the breakout level at $38.77 for the past few days. This suggests strong accumulation by the bulls as they anticipate the rally to resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/6f64933f-f023-4694-a810-b579b68bbb5b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the RSI just below the overbought territory indicate that buyers have the upper hand. A break and close above $44.78 could push the price to the all-time high at $49.78.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($37.84), it will suggest that bears have made a strong comeback. The DOT/USDT pair could then drop to the 50-day SMA ($33.63).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cointelegraph-consulting-etfs-listed-what-s-next-for-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Consulting: ETFs listed \u8212\'20\'14 What\u8217\'20\'19s next for Bitcoin?}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line on Oct. 18 but could not sustain the higher levels as seen from the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The buyers again tried to clear the overhead hurdle at the downtrend line on Oct. 19 but failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/07d169a0-5e84-49c6-969b-2e26f356f65c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 After twice being unsuccessful, the bulls are again trying to drive and sustain the price above the downtrend line today. Such a move will invalidate the developing descending triangle pattern, clearing the path for a possible rally to $0.32 and then $0.35.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the downtrend line and breaks below the 20-day EMA ($0.23), it will suggest that bears are aggressively defending the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below the 20-day EMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the strong support zone at $0.21 to $0.19.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token broke below the 50-day SMA ($36.66) on Oct. 17 but the bears could not pull the price below the strong support at $34.86. The failure to do so seems to have attracted buying from aggressive bulls who have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $39.75 today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/ec57d2a8-b977-4de4-8168-d586424589ad.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LUNA/USDT pair could now rise to $45.01 where the bears are likely to offer a stiff resistance. If the price turns down from this level but rebounds off the breakout level at $39.75, it will suggest that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above $45.01 could push the pair to the all-time high at $49.54. On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $39.75, it will signal strong selling at higher levels. The pair could then drop to $34.86.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ) has been trading in a tight range between the neckline of the possible inverse H&S and the 20-day EMA ($25.32). This indicates indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5289e5dc-2cf0-48f9-b3bc-c247595b6b05.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the neckline will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. The UNI/USDT pair could then rally to $31.41 and if this level is crossed, the up-move may reach the pattern target at $36.98.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level and plummets below the moving averages, the decline may extend to $22. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break below it could sink the pair to $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvMDUzMzk1MzctYTQyNS00YTk1LTkwYzMtOWI5YjRiZDE1NjhiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211020ehak000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/18: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,811 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Altcoins are selling off ahead of this week\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  launch, perhaps a sign that traders are anxious about this historic listing.\par \par \uc2 ProShares Bitcoin Strategy exchange-traded fund (ETF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/proshares-bitcoin-etf-to-debut-on-nyse-on-oct-19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will enter the history books on Oct. 19}}}\uc2  when it starts trading on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker BITO.\par \par \uc2 Market participants are likely to watch the volumes on the ETF closely to gauge the amount of participation from institutional investors. If the response is tepid for a few days, short-term traders may be tempted to book profits, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may pick up further if demand remains strong.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/a5155b64-c161-4bec-ae18-8886ccb93aa2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 The latest \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  report for the week ending Oct. 17 shows that i {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-managers-hold-a-record-72-3b-of-crypto-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nstitutional inflows into crypto products}}}\uc2  have pushed the total assets held by institutional managers to a new record high of $72.3 billion. Of the total inflow of $80 million during the week, Bitcoin products attracted the lion\u8217\'20\'19s share at $70 million.\par \par \uc2 Could the launch of a new ETF boost sentiment and push Bitcoin to a new all-time high or will short-term traders book profits? Is it time for money to flow out of Bitcoin and into altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s Oct. 17 candlestick shows strong buying on dips. The bulls attempted to push the price above the Oct. 15 high at $62,933 on Oct. 18 but failed. This suggests that bears are defending the zone between $62,933 and $64,854 with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/f7ce6987-666b-4044-bd3e-b55a2ac4b6bd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If sellers sink the price below $58,963, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the 20-week exponential moving average (EMA) ($55,118). A strong rebound off this support will indicate that sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead obstacle. If they succeed, the pair could start the next leg of the uptrend that could reach $70,000 and then $75,000.\par \par \uc2 If the 20-day EMA support is breached, the pair could drop to the breakout level at $52,920. This is an important support to keep an eye on because if it cracks, the pair may plummet to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($49,270).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully defended the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern on Oct. 17 but they could not sustain the rebound. This suggests that demand dries up at higher levels. The bears pulled Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) to the neckline of the setup again on Oct. 18.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/391895e5-b5e2-4d8f-8885-18ecfab982b3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break below the neckline could result in a decline to the 20-day EMA ($3,563). The rising moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive territory indicate that buyers have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA with strength, it will suggest that traders continue to accumulate on dips. The buyers will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at $4,027.88.\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the ETH/USDT pair could retest the all-time high at $4,372.72. Alternatively, if bears sink the price below the moving averages, the pair could correct to $3,200.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to take off after completing the inverse H&S pattern on Oct. 13 but a minor positive is that bulls have not allowed the price to sustain below the neckline of the setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/bae92d32-9e96-4ddf-ae17-5955f3e08afc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($439) is rising and the RSI is above 64, signaling that the path of least resistance is to the upside. If bulls push the price above $484.70, the BNB/USDT pair could rise to $518.90.\par \par \uc2 This level may act as a stiff resistance but if bulls overcome this obstacle, the pair could rally to the pattern target at $554.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest that bears are back in the game. The pair could then drop to $392.20.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is trading inside a symmetrical triangle pattern, which suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/9771061d-3757-4bfb-85bc-392384477361.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($2.20) is sloping down gradually and the RSI has dropped near 43, suggesting a minor advantage to bears. If sellers sink the piece below the support line of the triangle, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to $1.87.\par \par \uc2 This level could attract strong buying from the bulls. A breakout and close above the resistance line of the triangle will indicate that bulls have absorbed the supply and made a strong comeback.\par \par \uc2 The pair could then rally to $2.47, which may act as a resistance but if the bulls overcome this obstacle, the up-move may extend to $2.80.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple's ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) attempt to rise above the overhead resistance at $1.24 fizzled out at $1.18 on Oct. 16. This may have attracted profit-booking by short-term traders, resulting in a drop below the moving averages on Oct. 17.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/0f53da2b-a7b6-4cfe-803e-c5141b6b4b7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that bulls are aggressively defending the psychological level at $1. Both moving averages have flattened out and the RSI is near the midpoint, suggesting a range-bound action in the short term.\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USDT pair could consolidate between $1 and $1.24 for a few days. A break and close above $1.24 could clear the path for a possible up-move to $1.41 while a drop below $1 may pull the pair down to $0.85.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) has been sustaining above the downtrend line for the past three days but the bulls are struggling to start an up-move. This suggests that bears have not thrown in the towel yet and are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1275375f-7b85-4798-be37-25f174a91654.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears pull and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA ($151), the SOL/USDT pair could drop to $137.61. A break and close below this support could clear the path for a further decline to the important level at $116.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the current level and sustains above $167.65, it will suggest that buyers are back in the game. The pair could thereafter rally to the 61.80% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) broke above the $38.77 overhead resistance on Oct. 13 but the bulls could not capitalize on this strength. This indicates that bears are unwilling to relent and are selling on every rise.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/3f2d625c-229c-4df2-9160-ade344070521.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a drop and close below the breakout level at $38.77 and the 20-day EMA ($36.64). The DOT/USDT pair could then drop to the 50-day SMA ($33.05).\par \par \uc2 The uptrending 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive zone indicate that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level or $38.77 and breaks above $44.78, it will suggest that bulls are back in the game. The pair may then retest the all-time high at $49.78.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/2021/10/18/lushsux-ass-whoopins-nft-street-art-christies-auction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lushsux: A decade of ass-whoopin\u8217\'20\'19 and skullduggery in a single NFT}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears pulled the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.23) on Oct. 17 but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests accumulation at lower levels. Strong buying on Oct. 18 pushed \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/d1c91dcd-2a55-445c-a13f-005ff589beff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Oct. 18\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that bears are defending the downtrend line aggressively. If bulls fail to sustain the price above the downtrend line, the DOGE/USDT pair could again drop to $0.21.\par \pa