comparison, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-managers-hold-a-record-57b-worth-of-crypto-according-to-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional crypto holdings were worth $57 billion}}}\uc2  in March and reached $71.6 billion in May.\par \par \uc2 For the latest week, \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products saw inflows totaling $80 million. Bitcoin products attracted the largest investments at $70 million, marking the fifth consecutive week of inflows. Institutional investors also increased their holdings of Polkadot (DOT) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) products by $3.6 million and $2.7 million, respectively. Meanwhile, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) products saw minor outflows totaling $1 million.\par \par \uc2 In terms of provider, \uc2 ETC Group\uc2  and \uc2 21Shares\uc2  saw the largest weekly inflows at $63.6 million and $19.3 million, respectively. Inflows into Grayscale products, which represent the largest crypto-focused funds, flat-lined.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is coming off its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-eyes-all-time-high-weekly-close-above-60k-ahead-of-bitcoin-etf-turbulence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest weekly close on record}}}\uc2 , as the spot price came within striking distance of $63,000 on Friday. The largest cryptocurrency by market capitalization is rising in anticipation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-proshares-follows-valkyrie-in-approval-for-listing-bitcoin-strategy-etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two futures-based exchange-traded funds (ETFs) hitting the market}}}\uc2  in the near future. The ProShares Bitcoin Strategy ETF is scheduled to begin trading on the New York Stock Exchange on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-hints-at-plans-to-convert-bitcoin-trust-into-btc-settled-etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grayscale hints at plans to convert Bitcoin trust into BTC-settled ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  listing in the United States could attract new investors to the cryptocurrency market by giving them a familiar and highly regulated vehicle in which to park their assets. ProShares CEO Michael Sapir {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/10/18/first-bitcoin-futures-etf-to-make-its-debut-on-the-nyse-tuesday-proshares-says.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Monday that investors have been \u8220\'20\'1Ceagerly awaiting the launch\u8221\'20\'1D of a Bitcoin-focused ETF.\par \par \uc2 Pent-up demand among traditional investors was reflected in the recently launched Canadian Bitcoin ETFs, which attracted inflows of billions shortly after launching. The \uc2 Purpose Bitcoin ETF\uc2 , which launched in February, now has $1.7 billion in assets under management, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bybt.com/etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to Bybt data.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvY2M5NjU5NDAtN2Y1ZS00MGU2LWE1N2UtMjc2MWIzYTg1ODcwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211018ehai000bd\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 The responsibility behind a crypto lender\u8217\'20\'19s asset listing\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Magdalena Hristova \par \uc2 1,687 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Responsibility in crypto lending will pave the way towards an ethically and morally guided financial future rather than one based on profit.\par \par \uc2 Crypto lenders are the institutions situated between consumers and the untamed, blockchain-based, and often unregulated space of cryptocurrencies. As such, they are in a peculiar position when it comes to responsibility towards their customers and the assets for which they provide services. Consequently, when choosing which currencies to support, lenders lead a delicate dance of responsibility, a balancing act between catering to popular demand and adding cryptocurrencies that are sustainable, worthwhile and safe.\par \par \uc2 Demand vs. approval: The question of endorsement\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unsurprising that in a nascent industry full of new investors, a lender\u8217\'20\'19s asset integration is often taken for endorsement. What tends to be overlooked when companies add new assets to their range of services is that crypto lending is, in fact, a business, and any asset integration is ultimately a response to demand \u8212\'20\'14 a good market opportunity that generates gains for business and clients, alike. Perhaps this is due to lenders being influential entities in a space that has historically lacked the institutional stamp of approval and looks for it through the pioneering businesses shaping the industry.\par \par \uc2 In June 2021, Coinbase CEO \uc2 Brian Armstrong{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brian_armstrong/status/1409555698942238723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1409555698942238723%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fdecrypt.co%2F74652%2Fcoinbase-rapidly-adding-new-assets-for-trading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  a series of tweets concerning the exchange\u8217\'20\'19s rapid integration of multiple assets and its intention to keep up this pace. Armstrong wrote that \u8220\'20\'1Cone should not take being listed on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  as an endorsement of that asset\u8221\'20\'1D, denoting the fine discrepancy between working with an asset and endorsing it. Even though their operations are different from that of an exchange, the same principle applies to crypto lenders: It is not an endorsement, it\u8217\'20\'19s just business. And there are many ways to create client-centric and socially responsible businesses.\par \par \uc2 If not an endorsement, then what?\par \par \uc2 Listing an asset on a lending platform may not be an endorsement but it is an indication of a certain degree of its legitimacy, stability and security. A crypto lender\u8217\'20\'19s operations with a given coin mean that owning it, investing with/in it and using financial services for it is regulatorily and technically sound. Lenders have a lot to lose from working with unreliable cryptocurrencies including funds as well as their customers\u8217\'20\'19 trust and the future of their business; hence, they maintain high standards for an asset\u8217\'20\'19s technical robustness, market-wide liquidity, price stability and legality. While the due diligence of these companies cannot serve as the aforementioned stamp of approval for investors, they can be a crypto wind indicator of sorts, providing a general indication of an asset\u8217\'20\'19s stability and safety without endorsing it.\par \par \uc2 Crypto lenders have thus become the bellwether for regulatory action and it is worth noting that this intricate inter-dependence goes both ways \u8212\'20\'14 suspending services for cryptocurrencies immediately upon even the potential for new regulatory issues with a coin or token. This exact scenario played out on December 23, 2020, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/xrp-price-falls-24-in-24-hours-as-exchanges-begin-delisting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple major exchanges and crypto lenders}}}\uc2  halted their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  services in light of the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-unveils-1-3b-suit-against-ripple-over-xrp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission lawsuit of Ripple Labs}}}\uc2 . The valuable takeaway is that these institutions\u8217\'20\'19 immediate reactions to even the possibility of legal issues with XRP demonstrate a tendency towards full compliance, competent legal counsel, and readiness for immediate action in accordance with given circumstances. Essentially, responsible crypto companies are the industry\u8217\'20\'19s first reactors and can be useful to watch when navigating the space.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-vs-ripple-a-predictable-but-undesirable-development"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC vs. Ripple: A predictable but undesirable development}}}\par \par \uc2 Listings and the [Insert company name] effect\par \par \uc2 Although coin integrations on lending platforms do not denote endorsement, companies\u8217\'20\'19 actions still have a strong collateral effect on cryptocurrencies. The biggest crypto exchanges in the world both have their respective so-called \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Coinbase\uc2 -effect\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CBinance-effect\u8221\'20\'1D that cause newly-listed coins to appreciate significantly in value. On one hand, this is because they suddenly become available to a wider audience of investors but in addition, their inclusion by these exchange giants gives buyers a sense of credibility.\par \par \uc2 A similar phenomenon was observed in 2020 when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-to-offer-crypto-payments-starting-in-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PayPal announced its plans to operate}}}\uc2  with Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ): News spread quickly and had an overall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/here-s-what-traders-expect-after-bitcoin-price-rallied-to-13-217"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uplifting effect}}}\uc2  on the market. This year, the predominant example was the \u8220\'20\'1CTesla-\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1CElon-effect\u8221\'20\'1D which began with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/elon-musk-says-tesla-now-accepts-bitcoin-from-us-customers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla accepting Bitcoin as payment}}}\uc2  for its vehicles in March 2021 and then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-loses-6-in-an-hour-after-tesla-drops-payments-over-carbon-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retracting this opportunity}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 needless to say, both actions caused a ripple in the crypto industry. A couple of months later, Elon Musk, himself, arguably triggered a market downturn that lasted nearly two months with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-slumps-2k-on-musk-s-in-the-end-tweets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a single tweet}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/experts-answer-how-does-elon-musk-affect-crypto-space"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Experts answer: How does Elon Musk affect crypto space?}}}\par \par \uc2 These examples of non-crypto native companies\u8217\'20\'19 influence on crypto prices are not even close to exhaustive and portray the sway big brands can have on the volatile crypto market. They signal a need for responsibility on part of all companies operating in the blockchain space, especially for crypto lenders who are set to become the banks of the new financial system. It is a volatile market with many smaller retail investors and new players. In the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the industry must self-regulate, recognizing and moderating the gravity of their listings, investments, statements and even tweets.\par \par \uc2 The technical side of listing assets\par \par \uc2 Generally speaking, there are two main approaches to adding new assets to crypto lending platforms. The first is a full blockchain integration and the second is a more internal-facing implementation. The former, enables users to deposit and withdraw assets from their wallets, giving them more overall flexibility. The trade-off is that such integrations take slightly longer, require scarce tech talent, and depend on finding appropriate and reliable third-party custodians to ensure the complete security of assets at all times.\par \par \uc2 The alternative to full integration is an approach akin to \uc2 Revolut\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crypto offering wherein users may purchase cryptocurrencies and digital assets only on the lender\u8217\'20\'19s platform, cannot withdraw them to an external wallet and therefore don\u8217\'20\'19t have access to their private keys. Behind the scenes, the provider deals with the assets in their client\u8217\'20\'19s name, producing user-friendly exposure to crypto investments that can be implemented on the crypto lender\u8217\'20\'19s platform much faster than a standard integration. While \uc2 Revolut\uc2  has received criticism from the crypto community that prompted them to finally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/revolut-app-announces-bitcoin-withdrawals-within-limits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launch limited Bitcoin withdrawals}}}\uc2  in May 2021, this method has intrinsic value in a space as dynamic as blockchain finance and it\u8217\'20\'19s why lenders like ours have taken on this adoption-friendly model for assets like Polkadot (DOT), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ), and the latest addition of Solana (SOL).\par \par \uc2 True to its struggle for ultimate security, the crypto community\u8217\'20\'19s famous mantra of \u8220\'20\'1Cnot your key\u8217\'20\'19s not your coins\u8221\'20\'1D was a natural hurdle for internal integrations. Regardless, they are flourishing on Nexo with $11, $28 and $12 million in turnovers from DOT, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  and DOGE purchases, respectively, within the first month of launching these integrations. Despite not being able to self-custody their assets, clients use them extensively. People want and need exposure to the new assets popping up regularly in the rapidly growing space. Crypto lenders simply can\u8217\'20\'19t keep up with this demand when using only the slower and exceedingly more resource-heavy blockchain integrations that give clients more control over assets, thus limiting exposure to many novel and well-performing coins.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot your keys, not your coins\u8221\'20\'1D embodies one of the essential benefits of crypto \u8212\'20\'14 the chance to take custody and security of your funds into your own hands rather than having to trust an institution. But perhaps the phrase is becoming slightly reductive as crypto begins to scale swiftly. For lenders and other companies using internal asset integrations, this strategy ought to be a springboard towards full integrations, a means through which to keep up with the industry, grow their business and give their clients timely exposure to lucrative investment opportunities.\par \par \uc2 The way forward: Social duties > Legal obligations\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, crypto lenders must mitigate the messages behind their asset listings, delicately weigh the words and actions behind their brands, and use different methods of integration to enhance their users\u8217\'20\'19 experience in the dynamic industry. In an environment lacking regulations and common standards due to its nascence, a lot of these actions depend mainly on crypto companies\u8217\'20\'19 social responsibility and blockchain-based corporate social responsibility (CSR).\par \par \uc2 This can include: 1) proactively shaping \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  for crypto as we have seen industry leaders do with regards to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-language-in-the-infrastructure-bill-is-a-political-shell-game-says-cointelegraph-gc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the pending U.S. Infrastructure Bill}}}\uc2  ; 2) presenting audits of reserves as Nexo has done through its real-time attest via Armanino; or 3) educating customers \u8212\'20\'14 through articles, ask-me-anything sessions, support groups, even metaverse worlds \u8212\'20\'14 about the assets they work with, the services they offer, and how to use them safely and advantageously.\par \par \uc2 Developing, unclear \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is something with which most industries have not dealt. Hence, the novel value behind crypto lenders and blockchain companies assuming more social responsibility and self-regulatory roles from the get-go is in the potential to create a more refined ecosystem with healthier relationships between clients, businesses and regulators. As crypto companies mature from start-ups to institutions with serious gravitas in blockchain and beyond, these principles of self-\b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and socially-minded services pave the way towards an ethically and morally guided financial world rather than one based solely on profit and legal obligations.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 Magdalena Hristova is a public relations manager at Nexo. With her penchant for writing and natural curiosity towards anything technically complex and equipped to cause ripples in incumbent industries, she began working as a copywriter in the crypto industry before migrating into the novel space of communications in crypto.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvOTMwNTVjMTgtM2NiYS00N2MwLTlmMGEtNTIyOTE1ZDVmYjBkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211016ehag0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/15: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,861 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Hopes of a BTC \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent Bitcoin charging toward a new all-time high and several altcoins are also breaking out of \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setups.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) rose within a few steps of $63,000 today for the first time since April 18. The recent surge in the price may have been caused after various documents pointed to the eventual approval of a futures-based BTC ETF by the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 . According to these documents, the regulator may be close to green lighting the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-nasdaq-listing-hints-that-the-sec-may-soon-approve-etf-application-from-valkyrie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 application}}}\uc2  to list Valkyrie\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin Strategy exchange-traded fund ETF for listing on Nasdaq.\par \par \uc2 Analysts pointed out that gold\u8217\'20\'19s price had risen sharply leading up to the launch of the first U.S.-based gold ETF in 2004. Thereafter, the rally continued and gold\u8217\'20\'19s price rose more than 300% since the ETF was approved, before forming a major top. The similarity between gold and Bitcoin being stores of value appear to have generated huge excitement for the launch of a \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/d83a1490-9c7a-4255-abd2-65e306ac7b17.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Traders seem to have aggressively accumulated Bitcoin before the announcement of a \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2 . The Bitcoin futures open interest in the Chicago Mercantile Exchange {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cme-bitcoin-futures-open-interest-hits-8-month-high-greater-than-when-btc-price-was-at-65k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit a new all-time high}}}\uc2  on Oct. 14, surpassing the previous high of $3.02 billion made on April 14.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin break above the all-time high and continue its northward journey and will altcoins also join the party? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Oct. 14, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears above the $58,000 level. This uncertainty resolved to the upside today and the rally has resumed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1d0b2014-da73-4804-bf32-752d345631d3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($52,868) is sloping up and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the overbought zone, suggesting that bulls are in control. However, the all-time high at $64,854 may prove to be a difficult hurdle to cross.\par \par \uc2 If the BTC/USDT pair turns down from this resistance, the first support to watch on the downside is the 20-day EMA. A strong rebound off this support will suggest that sentiment remains positive and traders are buying the dips.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the possibility of the resumption of the uptrend with the target at $75,000. The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 20-day EMA, which could result in a decline to the 50-day simple moving average ($48,514).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($3,479) on Oct. 13 and broke above the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern on Oct. 14. This completed the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup which has a target objective at $4,657.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/2e4f10fe-3427-4f70-8d1d-90e3ef9c09e4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI has broken above the downtrend line, suggesting that bulls are back in control. The ETH/USDT pair could now rally to $4,027.88 and then retest the all-time high at $4,372.72.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the neckline, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. The pair could then drop to the moving averages. A break and close below $3,257 will indicate that bulls may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the neckline on Oct. 13, completing an inverse H&S pattern. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a pattern target at $554.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/ecbea0e2-6bfa-4828-b8bd-7ae304c0ffff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears attempted to pull the price back below the breakout level but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates buying at lower levels. The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the positive zone, indicating that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the price rises from the current level and breaks above $518.90, it will signal the resumption of the uptrend. The bears will have to pull and sustain the BNB/USDT pair below the moving averages to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) back into the symmetrical triangle pattern but the bears are not relenting. They are defending the support line and the 20-day EMA ($2.21) with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/a33d5b77-1dcd-4aad-a604-55970a9d18dc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $2.07, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to $2 and next to $1.87. A breach below this important level may pull the pair down to the pattern target of $1.63\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bulls push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the resistance line of the triangle. A breakout and close above the triangle could clear the path for a rally to $2.47, followed by a move to $2.80.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has been holding above the 20-day EMA ($1.08) for the past few days but the bulls have not been able to push the price to the overhead resistance at $1.24. This suggests a shortage of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c7882368-212d-4d19-9a51-40f45cd3c15b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to $1. This level could again attract buyers but if they fail to push the price above $1.24, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up and the slide could deepen to $0.85.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level and breaks above $1.24, it will signal that the selling pressure may be easing. The pair could then rise to $1.41 and if bulls clear this barrier, the next stop could be $1.66.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sink Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) below the 50-day SMA ($147) in the past few days indicates accumulation by the bulls. The buyers are currently attempting to sustain the price above the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/01d05a34-b6cc-4ef3-b539-68ef52734446.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80. This level may act as stiff resistance but if bulls overcome this hurdle, the pair may rally to $200 and then retest the all-time high at $216.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 50-day SMA. That could pull the price down to $116. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break below it could intensify the selling.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) skyrocketed and closed above the $38.77 overhead resistance on Oct. 13, suggesting that the consolidation has resolved in favor of the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/d89cdb17-2c2d-4d06-8495-ce112677b1ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears tried to pull the price back below $38.77 on Oct. 14 and today but failed. This shows that buyers are aggressively defending the breakout level. If bulls drive the price above $43.22, the DOT/USDT pair could retest the all-time high at $49.78.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $38.77, the pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($34.84). A strong bounce off this support will suggest that sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bears sink the price below the moving averages, the pair could drop to $25.50. Such a move will suggest that the breakout above $38.77 may have been a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cftc-slaps-tether-and-bitfinex-with-a-combined-42-5-million-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CFTC slaps Tether and Bitfinex with a combined $42.5 million fine}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to sustain \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.23), which suggests that buying dries up at higher levels. A minor positive is that bulls have not allowed the price to sustain below $0.22.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/92f0b9fa-0aab-497c-8d73-cf1fa949d56f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, suggesting a balance between supply and demand. This equilibrium will tilt in favor of the bears if the $0.21 support cracks. That may result in a decline to $0.19.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from the current level, the bulls will try to push the price to the downtrend line. A breakout and close above this level will suggest that the decline could be over. The DOGE/USDT pair may next rise to $0.32 and then to $0.35.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token is finding support at the 50-day SMA ($36.24) for the past three days but the bulls have not been able to drive the price above the 20-day EMA ($38.86). This suggests that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/da41cd80-e6ff-443e-8a7b-92ac56693b41.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is sloping down marginally and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a minor advantage to bears. A break and close below the 50-day SMA could pull the price down to $32.50 and if this support cracks, the correction could deepen to $25.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the LUNA/USDT pair could pick up momentum and advance to $45.01 where bears may again try to mount a stiff resistance. A retest of the all-time high at $49.54 is likely if bulls overcome this obstacle.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ) rose above the moving averages on Oct. 13 and reached the neckline of the inverse H&S pattern on Oct. 14. The bears are currently attempting to stall the recovery at the neckline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/4dfbffff-b519-4eed-b606-3686a81e3060.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI has climbed into the positive territory, indicating that bulls have the upper hand. If the price rebounds off the moving averages, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the UNI/USDT pair above the neckline.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will complete the inverse H&S setup, starting a possible rally to $31.41 and later to the pattern target at $36.98. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate if the price continues lower and breaks below $22. The pair could then drop to the strong support at $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZjZjZjRlOTgtNGZkNi00NTkxLTkyZTEtNjdmYzY1NThjYjk3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211016ehag00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin analyst \u8216\'20\'18highly doubts\u8217\'20\'19 return to $50K \u8212\'20\'14 Will the weekly close spark a correction?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 451 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 All eyes on the weekly close for Bitcoin as BTC price action nears historical resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) challenged brand-new support levels on Oct. 14 after overnight successes took the market past $58,000\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/50fc54a0-dd80-42ea-b13c-91d192913da2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin \u8220\'20\'1Cdips\u8221\'20\'1D to near $57,000\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  tracked BTC/USD as it reversed toward $57,000 after hitting highs of $58,540 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The moves mimicked the first time Bitcoin had attacked $58,000 in February \u8212\'20\'14 several attempts interspersed by consolidation, followed ultimately by a run to April\u8217\'20\'19s all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 Despite on-chain indicators showing that Bitcoin is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-eyes-big-58k-resistance-as-new-data-shows-hodlers-acting-the-opposite-to-q1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 different beast}}}\uc2  in Q4, however, the mood was just as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time around.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin is most likely just continuing this grind towards the all-time highs,\u8221\'20\'1D Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cryptomichnl/status/1448555039585443843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in his latest \uc2 Twitter\uc2  update.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreat bounce from $54K. Highly doubt we\u8217\'20\'19ll see a retest at $50K happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cementing $50,000 as support \u8212\'20\'14 albeit for a second time in 2021 \u8212\'20\'14 would form a clear signal on the market trajectory as pundits gear up for what they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/catch-the-bitcoin-dip-btc-price-pares-losses-with-a-fresh-surge-to-57k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expect}}}\uc2  to be an explosive end to the year.\par \par \uc2 For trader and analyst Rekt Capital, however, there was a potential cause for concern this week. Zooming out, BTC/USD has failed to close a weekly candle above $60,000, and a repeat performance could likewise spell a copycat correction.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  has successfully retested its Daily Bull Flag thus far\par \par \uc2 But Bitcoin is still below major Weekly resistance (red)\par \par \uc2 In fact, any sort of Weekly Close below $60000 has historically preceded a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  retrace from these highs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n9vFaaalVM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n9vFaaalVM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1448338538102149131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 That leaves bulls until Sunday to crack a historical watermark, something which may still be helped before Monday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-tickers-and-ark-filing-shows-bitcoin-futures-etf-approval-imminent-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approval decision}}}\uc2  on a futures-based exchange-traded fund.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot breakout headlines altcoin return\par \par \uc2 Altcoins, meanwhile, saw brief respite from weakness in the face of \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin season.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-10-13-btc-eth-bnb-ada-xrp-sol-doge-dot-luna-uni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 10/13: BTC, ETH, BNB, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI}}}\par \par \uc2 The exception was Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT, up 28% in a week on news that its auctions would finally begin next month \u8212\'20\'14 a key original feature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/polkadot-to-debut-parachain-auctions-after-governance-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five years}}}\uc2  in the making.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5b750651-6caf-4406-91d8-a7e882426a67.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD 1-hour candle chart (Kraken). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The largest altcoin, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), managed 5.3% daily gains, with all of the top 10 cryptocurrencies by market capitalization trading higher on the day as Bitcoin slowed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZTBmOWZiYmQtYWU1Mi00NzI3LWI2MzktMzllZmVhNzRhY2RlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrsl